---

Before modifying SPAAVS, read `SPAAVS_PRODUCT_REFERENCE.md` at the repository root. That file is the canonical product reference. Preserve its distinctions unless the user explicitly approves a change.

`SPAAVS_Master_Business_Investor_AI.zip` is confidential persistent memory. Only a master admin may retrieve or distribute it. Do not commit, deploy, or publish the archive or its financial figures. See `.cursor/rules/spaavs-master-business.mdc`.

- **SPAAVS Mobile App:** Customer-facing application for human drivers.
- **SPAAVS Fleet Hub:** The website commercial fleet operators use to subscribe to SPAAVS services, pay for them, and manage their autonomous vehicles. It is the fleet operator interface and the authorized system-to-system integration solution for parking, charging, tracking, appointments, and readiness. It replaces both SPAAVS Mobile Hub and SPAAVS Fleet API as branded names. Do not reintroduce either name. Where both retired names would appear, use one SPAAVS Fleet Hub reference.
- **SPAAVS Fleet Center:** A center at every facility, staffed by people on site. It is not the Fleet Hub website and not the SPAAVS Mobility Hub.
- **SPAAVS Mobility Hub:** Official name of the Azure-hosted SaaS technology stack. It is not a physical facility and not a substitute for the Fleet Hub. The Four-Tier Facility Development Model still uses this name for Tier 4. Do not rename that tier unless the user approves a change.
- **SPAAVS Core Platform Services:** Architectural component of the SPAAVS Mobility Hub, paired with SPAAVS Facility and Fleet Connectivity. Not a separately branded commercial product. These services remain authoritative for reservations, access, assignments, payments, and service coordination.
- **SPAAVS Facility and Fleet Connectivity:** Architectural component of the SPAAVS Mobility Hub, paired with SPAAVS Core Platform Services. Not a separately branded commercial product.
- **SPAAVS AI Intelligence Layer:** A shared layer inside the Azure SPAAVS Mobility Hub for the Mobile App, with a later path to the Fleet Hub. It covers voice and text assistance, predictive occupancy, consent-based personalization, proactive assistance, and headless workflow orchestration. It does not replace Core Platform Services or Facility and Fleet Connectivity, and it does not control a vehicle.
- APIs are underlying technical interfaces, not branded commercial products. Do not rename API endpoints, database identifiers, or internal software interfaces because of this branding change.
- **Integrated LiDAR and Camera Infrastructure:** Facility-based technology supporting vehicle identification, tracking, parking availability and indoor navigation. Do not imply that customer phones require LiDAR. BLE/UWB are contingency options, not baseline infrastructure.
- **Indoor Mapping Technology:** Spatial representation of participating facilities supporting navigation and route guidance.

Vehicle identification matches an arriving vehicle to its visit. Entry is confirmed with the reservation and authorized credentials. On public pages, explain it that way. Do not say that a license plate alone is not authorization. Autonomous driving remains under the vehicle manufacturer's control; SPAAVS coordinates facility services through authorized integrations and does not control vehicle motion.

Parking reservations and vehicle service appointments are optional for human drivers. Walk-ins are subject to availability and facility rules. Services can be requested at participating facilities or through the Mobile App, independently or together. No mandatory bundles or app-only service requirements. Preserve hands-free driver guidance: no handheld interaction while driving. The Mobile App is designed for a spoken, hands-free service request. Spoken indoor guidance uses facility cameras, LiDAR, and indoor mapping. Do not imply that the phone requires LiDAR.

Public AI copy describes intended capabilities, not a live deployment. Hands-free use reduces manual interaction and does not eliminate distraction. Drivers remain responsible for safe driving. Do not claim quantified safety results. Predictions are estimates. Do not publish AI prices or financial estimates. A paid request needs explicit authorization, and the app speaks success only after the platform confirms it. No model access to payment credentials. No autonomous vehicle control. Use validated routes and live sensor data. Say when facility data is missing or stale. Do not infer consent. Describe intended capabilities without claiming verified deployments, certifications, or partnerships.
